{"_id":"6ad7d179a4131568064faebb","id":"alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions","author":"alexar76","sha":"c5e7f6118c127e1e680692ab41956f1b28274570","lastModified":"2026-11-09T09:30:31.000Z","private":false,"gated":false,"disabled":false,"tags":["task_categories:text-classification","task_ids:multi-label-classification","annotations_creators:machine-generated","multilinguality:monolingual","source_datasets:original","language:en","license:cc-by-4.0","size_categories:100K<n<1M","format:json","modality:tabular","modality:text","library:datasets","library:pandas","library:polars","library:mlcroissant","region:us","mcp","model-context-protocol","ai-security","prompt-injection","tool-poisoning","transparency-log","supply-chain-security","ai-agents"],"description":"\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tHISTOR snapshot 2026-11-09: what MCP servers advertise, and when it changes\n\t\n\nHISTOR reads the tool list (tools/list) of every remote MCP server in the official MCP registry\non a polling schedule, and of npm/PyPI MCP packages run in a sandbox once per published version (new versions\nfirst, a few hundred a day). It records the exact tool definitions,\npins them by digest, and writes a signed label to a public RFC 9162 Merkle log whenever a tool set\nfirst appears, stays the same, or… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions.","downloads":230,"likes":0,"cardData":{"license":"cc-by-4.0","pretty_name":"HISTOR — MCP tool definitions and how they change","language":["en"],"task_categories":["text-classification"],"task_ids":["multi-label-classification"],"annotations_creators":["machine-generated"],"source_datasets":["original"],"multilinguality":["monolingual"],"tags":["mcp","model-context-protocol","ai-security","prompt-injection","tool-poisoning","transparency-log","supply-chain-security","ai-agents"],"size_categories":["100K<n<1M"],"configs":[{"config_name":"servers","data_files":"servers.jsonl.gz"},{"config_nam